 ```
 
+## Accounts and authentication
+
+Each person has an account and sees only their own tasks. Sign up, sign in, then send the token with every task request:
+
+```sh
+curl -X POST localhost:3000/api/users -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"username":"alice","password":"a long passphrase"}'
+curl -X POST localhost:3000/api/sessions -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"username":"alice","password":"a long passphrase"}'
+# {"token":"…"}
+curl localhost:3000/api/tasks -H 'Authorization: Bearer <token>'
+```
+
+- A username is lowercased, then must be 3 to 32 characters among `a-z`, `0-9` and `_`. It is unique whatever the case. A password has at least 10 characters.
+- Passwords are stored salted and hashed with scrypt (`node:crypto`) and compared in constant time. Signing in with an unknown username costs the same work as with a wrong password and gets the same answer.
+- A token is 32 random bytes from the OS (base64url). Only its SHA-256 is stored, so a leaked database holds no usable token. Tokens do not expire: they last until `DELETE /api/sessions`. A user may hold several at once (one per sign-in).
+- A task belongs to the user who created it. Another user's task answers `404 { "error": "task not found" }`, exactly like a task that does not exist. Tasks created before accounts existed (no owner) stay in the database and are never returned.
+- No response contains a password or a hash. JSON bodies are limited to 64 KiB.
+- Not covered: rate limiting of sign-in attempts, password reset, token expiry. Serve the app over HTTPS: tokens and passwords travel in clear text otherwise.
+
 ## API
 
 Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `POST /api/users` | Creates an account from `{ "username", "password" }` | 201 `{ "id", "username" }`; 400 `invalid username` or `password too short`; 409 `username taken` |
+| `POST /api/sessions` | Signs in with `{ "username", "password" }` | 201 `{ "token" }`; 401 `invalid credentials` (wrong username or password alike) |
+| `DELETE /api/sessions` | Signs out: the token stops working | 204, or 401 |
+
+The task routes need `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; a missing, malformed or unknown token answers 401 `{ "error": "authentication required" }`. They only ever see the tasks of the signed-in user.
+
+| Method and path | What it does | Answers |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists your tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` (a non-empty string) | 201, the task; 400 |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` (a boolean) | 200, the task, or 400, 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
 ## Layout
 
 - `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
-- `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
+- `src/tasks.ts`: the task queries, all scoped to the owner.
+- `src/users.ts`: accounts, password hashing, sessions and tokens.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
-- `public/`: the page.
+- `public/`: the page, with its sign-up / sign-in form; the token is kept in `localStorage`.
 - `test/`: the API tests, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
